Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:19:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 4126 item 3: people from public member lists get their own
 table
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

D757 point 2 (the founder's own) and Misho's yes (§133): list_people holds
what a public list says — name, organisation, listed role, source URL, the
day it was read. No phone of their own and no photo. A list says who belongs
to an organisation, never who knows whom: no row is a „knows" link or an
introduction route.

A row joins a known person (matched_phone) only through the same-name check:
exactly one candidate with the same full name AND the same organisation on
record; a shared name alone, or two candidates, leaves it unmerged.

Nothing writes to the table yet: loading a list is a write of live data and
waits for its own approval, as the Axel load did (4225). 6a's model-facing
sentence still needs Misho's yes.

